diff --git a/crates/rightkit-db/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-db/CHANGELOG.md
index 5300e3e..00f87a0 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-db/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-db/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.4 (2026-10-18)
+
+All additive; no existing item changed. Not compiled when written.
+
+- Additive: `MigrateHooks` with `with_backup_name`, `with_before_backup`, `with_verify_backup` and `with_retain_backups` (closures that may capture state), plus `migrate_with_hooks`, `DbOptions::open_writer_migrated_with_hooks` and `DbOptions::open_writer_migrated_or_degrade_with_hooks` (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#770). The `fn`-pointer fields on `MigrateOptions` cannot carry a key, a timestamp, a message count or a free-disk check. A hook that is set replaces the matching `MigrateOptions` field for that call (`backup_name`, `verify_backup`, `backup_retention`); `with_before_backup(|db, backup| ..)` is new and runs before the backup is written, so `Err(reason)` stops the migration as `DbError::Backup` with nothing written. The same plain-file-name and reserved-name checks apply to a hooked name. Closure type aliases `BackupNameHook`, `BeforeBackupHook`, `VerifyBackupHook`, `RetainBackupsHook` are exported. The `MigrateOptions` fields stay as they are, so no struct literal breaks. Tests in `tests/migrate_hooks.rs`.
+- Additive: `WalCheckpointJob::tick_min(conn, min_wal_bytes)`, `tick_min_at`, and `tick_min_frames(conn, min_frames)`: the PASSIVE minimum is given per call and replaces the policy's `passive_above_bytes` for that call (frames are turned into a lower bound in bytes from `PRAGMA page_size`) (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#769). `WalCheckpointJob::tick_passive_then_restart(conn, min_wal_bytes)` and `_at`, returning the new `WalCheckpointSequence { passive, restart }`: PASSIVE runs when the log is at least the minimum, and a RESTART follows in the same call only if that PASSIVE did not finish (busy, or fewer frames copied than the log holds) and the log is at least `restart_above_bytes` with the database idle for `quiet_for`. A PASSIVE that finished never escalates. All share the job's single-flight guard. `tick` and `tick_at` behave as before. Tests in `tests/checkpoint_job.rs`.
+- Additive: `ReadPool::readers_opened()`, the number of reader connections the pool has built (the first one included, shared by clones) (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#726). `ReadPool::from_opener` already lets a test count inside its own opener; for connections of every kind, count calls to the `DbOptions::init` hook, which runs once per connection opened, read-only pool readers included. Tests in `tests/read_pool.rs`.
+- Already present, no change in this release: `restore_database`, `restore_database_locked`, `recover_interrupted_restore` and `recover_interrupted_restore_locked` with a kept previous store, rollback and journal recovery (#451, 0.4.3); `replace_database` with `StoreLock` (#311, 0.4.3); `open_writer_migrated_or_degrade` with `RecoveryPolicy` stamp and sidecar options (#389, 0.4.3); `ReadPool::get_timeout` (#173), `remove_database_files` (#199), numbered `QuarantineStamp::Custom` retries (#541), the `write_pending_marker` writer (#608), and the MailRight items of #563 (`Zeroizing`, `write_txn_unchecked`, `ReadPool::from_opener`, backup name/verify/retention, `stored_version_is_newer`, `checkpoint_restart`), and `WalCheckpointJob` (#494).
+
 ## 0.4.3 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Fix: `recover_interrupted_restore` no longer drops the journal while sidecars of the previous store are still at the kept name. A stop between the renames of a put-back (main file back, `-wal`/`-shm`/`-journal` not yet) now resumes the sidecar moves whether or not the live main file exists; the journal goes only after every kept file is back, so committed WAL-only rows are not lost. Not compiled when written.
